;; groundwork's libraries, by side, and which others each may use.
;; test-code/groundwork/libraries_test.clj checks every namespace against it:
;; a library requires only the libraries it lists, and only their api;
;; nobody uses another around a circle. groundwork-shaped-json is a library of its own
;; (github.com/p4ulcristian/groundwork-shaped-json): any library may use it, through groundwork-shaped-json.api only.
;; So is groundwork-postgres, Postgres (github.com/p4ulcristian/groundwork-postgres): any server library
;; may use it, through groundwork-postgres.api only. So is groundwork-background-jobs, background jobs
;; (github.com/p4ulcristian/groundwork-background-jobs): any server library may use it, through
;; groundwork-background-jobs.api only. So is browser-build, the browser build and the stylesheets it
;; bundles (github.com/p4ulcristian/groundwork-browser-build): only to build, never in
;; production, so no server namespace requires it (main loads it only when it
;; watches, by requiring-resolve); a browser namespace names its stylesheets
;; through groundwork-browser-build.api only. So is bridge, how the browser and the server
;; talk, with a handler's steps and the routes (github.com/p4ulcristian/groundwork-bridge):
;; any library on either side may use it, through groundwork-bridge.api only. So is
;; groundwork-access, who is asking and what they may do, sessions and access
;; (github.com/p4ulcristian/groundwork-access): any server library may use it, through
;; groundwork-access.api only (and main's REPL tools groundwork-access.repl, asking as a named
;; person, which no app code does); a browser library too, for the shape of "what may I
;; do?"'s answer, which groundwork-access.api's browser half holds. So is groundwork-live-updates, a change to a table rings every open
;; screen, which asks again (github.com/p4ulcristian/groundwork-live-updates): any library on
;; either side may use it, through groundwork-live-updates.api only. So is groundwork-logs, the app's
;; log (github.com/p4ulcristian/groundwork-logs): any server library may use it, through
;; groundwork-logs.api only. So is groundwork-screens, the browser's screens over groundwork-live-updates's
;; question store, in re-frame (github.com/p4ulcristian/groundwork-screens): any browser
;; library may use it, through groundwork-screens.api only; re-frame.core beside it, for
;; its events and subscriptions. So is groundwork-languages, which language a request, a
;; page and an address are in (github.com/p4ulcristian/groundwork-languages): any library
;; on either side may use it, through groundwork-languages.api only. So are groundwork-file-storage, the
;; app's files (github.com/p4ulcristian/groundwork-file-storage), and groundwork-email, its email
;; (github.com/p4ulcristian/groundwork-email): any server library may use them, through
;; groundwork-file-storage.api and groundwork-email.api only. So is safe, the settings and their secrets
;; (github.com/p4ulcristian/groundwork-settings): the server's only, through groundwork-settings.api only; an
;; app loads its settings with it, and groundwork compares a secret token with it.
{:server  {:main #{}}
 :browser {:main #{}}}
